{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And the rabble.</b> These are the mixed multitude that gathered upon them when they went out from Egypt." "<b>And the children of Israel also sat and wept.</b> With them." "<b>Who will give us flesh to eat.</b> Did they have no flesh? But was it not already stated, ״וְגַם עֵרֶב רַב עָלָה אִתָּם וְצֹאן וּבָקָר״ (Exodus 12), and even if they ate them — was it not said at their entry into the land, ״וּמִקְנֶה רַב הָיָה לִבְנֵי רְאוּבֵן״ (Numbers 32)? Rather, they seek a pretext (Sifrei)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:17.412978478Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}